# GdkPixbuf Image Loader Modules file
#
# Deliberately empty: it registers no loader modules. linux/main.cc points
# GDK_PIXBUF_MODULE_FILE at this file so gdk-pixbuf never dlopen()s the *host*
# loader modules from /usr/lib/<triplet>/gdk-pixbuf-2.0/2.10.0/loaders/ into
# this bundle's own GTK stack. Mixing the two is what aborted 2.4.1 on any
# distro newer than the ubuntu-24.04 builder -- see the comment on
# isolate_gdk_pixbuf_loaders() in linux/main.cc.
#
# gdk-pixbuf's PNG and JPEG loaders are compiled into libgdk_pixbuf-2.0.so.0
# and stay available; only the dynamically loaded formats (svg, tiff, ico, ...)
# are dropped. Nothing in this app asks GTK to rasterize one: Flutter renders
# the whole UI and decodes its own images, and the Linux plugin set registers
# no native dialogs. Should that change, bundle the matching loader modules
# next to this file and list them here with absolute runtime paths instead of
# falling back to the host's.
